    answer: "Rain on the window is a background, not a soaking. Droplets and streaks belong on the glass. The ordinary adult inside has dry hair and dry shoulders unless the story is that they just came in. Light comes from that overcast window, cool on the glass, a little warmer in the room, with the window-side cheek brighter. The face stays sharp. The glass can be soft. Crop so the window and the dry shoulders are both in frame, and leave a quiet band above if you need a title. Models like to sprinkle the whole frame, which puts weather on the face and makes an indoor talking shot look like a leak. Those beads on the forehead are visible on a phone. Say where the water is allowed to be. Use a dry reference, generate, compare the hair, reject the soak, and regenerate. A realistic face still needs an AI label. A cartoon is a different case.",
